<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1553" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ag-grăvesco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adg-</span></b> ), ĕre,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v.
			inch.</i>, <i>to become heavy.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: propinquitate parti, Pac. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 486, 5</span></i> (Trag. Rel. p. 85
			Rib.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Fig.,
			of sickness, <i>to become violent</i>, <i>severe</i>, <i>dangerous</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne Philumenae magis morbus adgravescat,</span>”
				<i>grow worse</i>, <i>be aggravated</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Hec. 3, 2, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
